<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sakuradamon Incident</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sakuradamon Incident was the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ii-naosuke">Ii Naosuke</a>, chief minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a>, on 24 March 1860 outside the Sakurada Gate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-castle">Edo Castle</a>. The killers, mostly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> from Mito, opposed his signing of trade treaties with Western powers without imperial approval and his purge of opponents. The killing badly weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>.</p></div>
